+ # Operation Blue Tiger milestone 2
+ blue_tiger.1.t: "The Inauguration"
+ blue_tiger.1.d_green: "On 20 May 2000, power passes from the Kuomintang to the Democratic Progressive Party for the first time. The new president takes the oath before a crowd that once could not have imagined it, while Beijing and Washington listen closely to every word of the inaugural address."
+ blue_tiger.1.d_blue: "On 20 May 2000, the Republic of China inaugurates its second directly elected president. The handover keeps the government in Pan-Blue hands, but the campaign showed how much the electorate has changed since 1996."
+ blue_tiger.1.a: "Pledge the Four Noes"
+ blue_tiger.1.b: "Stand on our mandate"
+ blue_tiger.1.c: "Promise continuity and reconciliation"
+ blue_tiger.2.t: "The 2000 Transfer of Power"
+ blue_tiger.2.d: "For half a century the officer corps served a state run by the Kuomintang. Now its commander-in-chief comes from the party many senior officers were trained to distrust. How the new government handles its first appointments will shape civil-military relations for years."
+ blue_tiger.2.a: "Reassure the commanders"
+ blue_tiger.2.b: "Appoint reform-minded officers"
+ blue_tiger.2.c: "Insist on constitutional practice"
+ blue_tiger.3.t: "The Dot-Com Bust"
+ blue_tiger.3.d: "The collapse of global technology demand has hit our export economy hard. Factory orders are falling, unemployment is climbing above anything seen in decades, and the economy is heading for its first annual contraction since the island's industrialisation."
+ blue_tiger.3.a: "Fund a stimulus package"
+ blue_tiger.3.b: "Let the market correct itself"
+ blue_tiger.4.t: "The 2001 Legislative Election"
+ blue_tiger.4.d: "Voters have redrawn the Legislative Yuan. The Kuomintang has lost its position as the largest party, James Soong's People First Party has won dozens of seats, and Lee Teng-hui's new Taiwan Solidarity Union has entered the chamber on the Pan-Green side."
+ blue_tiger.4.a: "The new legislature takes its seats"
+ blue_tiger.5.t: "SARS Reaches Taiwan"
+ blue_tiger.5.d: "A new respiratory illness that began in Guangdong has reached our hospitals. Cases are rising, a Taipei hospital has been sealed with staff and patients inside, and we still have no direct line to the World Health Organization."
+ blue_tiger.5.a: "Impose strict quarantine"
+ blue_tiger.5.b: "Keep the economy open"
+ blue_tiger.6.t: "Shots on Election Eve"
+ blue_tiger.6.d: "On the final day of the campaign, the president and vice president have been wounded by gunshots while campaigning in Tainan. Both are recovering, but with the vote tomorrow, rumour and suspicion are spreading faster than the investigators can work."
+ blue_tiger.6.a: "Call for calm and let investigators work"
+ blue_tiger.7.t: "A Margin of Thousands"
+ blue_tiger.7.d: "The incumbent has won by fewer than thirty thousand votes out of thirteen million. The opposition demands a recount and has filed suit, and protesters fill the streets outside the Presidential Office."
+ blue_tiger.7.a: "Accept a full recount and court review"
+ blue_tiger.7.b: "Declare the result final"
+ blue_tiger.8.t: "The Anti-Secession Law"
+ blue_tiger.8.d: "The National People's Congress has passed a law authorising \"non-peaceful means\" if Taiwan moves toward independence, if a major incident leads to separation, or if the possibility of peaceful unification is exhausted. Beijing alone will decide when those conditions are met."
+ blue_tiger.8.a: "Rally in the streets"
+ blue_tiger.8.b: "Work quietly with Washington"
+ blue_tiger.8.c: "Appeal to the world"
+ blue_tiger.9.t: "The Journey of Peace"
+ blue_tiger.9.d: "The Kuomintang chairman has travelled to Beijing and met the General Secretary of the Communist Party, the first meeting of the two parties' leaders since the civil war. The opposition is now conducting its own cross-Strait diplomacy."
+ blue_tiger.9.a: "Condemn the visit"
+ blue_tiger.9.b: "Welcome any step toward dialogue"
+ blue_tiger.9.c: "Let the voters judge"
+ blue_tiger.10.t: "The State Affairs Fund"
+ blue_tiger.10.d_audited: "Prosecutors are examining how the president's discretionary State Affairs Fund was spent. Because the fund was audited and our party's finances were opened earlier, the inquiry is narrow, but the opposition is eager to make the most of it."
+ blue_tiger.10.d_open: "Prosecutors are examining how the president's discretionary State Affairs Fund was spent, and allegations now reach members of the first family. The case is unproven, but it is consuming the government's credibility day by day."
+ blue_tiger.10.a: "Cooperate with the prosecutors"
+ blue_tiger.10.b: "Resist the investigation"
+ blue_tiger.11.t: "The Red Shirts"
+ blue_tiger.11.d: "Hundreds of thousands of protesters in red have surrounded the Presidential Office, demanding the president's resignation over the corruption allegations. A recall motion is moving through the Legislative Yuan."
+ blue_tiger.11.a: "Respect the right to protest"
+ blue_tiger.11.b: "Call counter-rallies in the south"
+ blue_tiger.12.t: "The 2008 Legislative Election"
+ blue_tiger.12.d_sntv: "The first election under single-member districts has reshaped the Legislative Yuan. The new system rewards the largest party in each district, and the results are lopsided."
+ blue_tiger.12.d_old: "Voters have returned a new Legislative Yuan after a campaign dominated by the economy and fatigue with the governing party."
+ blue_tiger.12.a: "The opposition sweeps the districts"
+ blue_tiger.12.b: "Our majority is renewed"
+ blue_tiger.13.t: "Democracy's Second Test"
+ blue_tiger.13.d: "The newly elected president is inaugurated on 20 May 2008. Whatever the outcome, eight years after the first transfer of power, alternation in office has become part of ordinary politics on the island."
+ blue_tiger.13.a: "A second peaceful turnover"
+ blue_tiger.13.b: "The mandate continues"
+ blue_tiger.20.t: "Reconciliation Talks"
+ blue_tiger.20.d: "Emissaries from Lien Chan and James Soong are meeting quietly to discuss a joint campaign. Soong's supporters left the party bitterly, and neither man wants to be the one who steps aside."
+ blue_tiger.20.a: "Await the outcome"
+ blue_tiger.21.t: "Choosing a Premier"
+ blue_tiger.21.d: "The president must nominate a premier who can work with the Legislative Yuan. A respected figure from across the aisle would calm the opposition and the officer corps; a trusted party colleague would push the government's programme harder."
+ blue_tiger.21.a: "Nominate a cross-party premier"
+ blue_tiger.21.b: "Nominate a party loyalist"
+ blue_tiger.22.t: "The Fourth Nuclear Plant Crisis"
+ blue_tiger.22.d: "The Lungmen nuclear plant is budgeted and partly built. Halting it would honour years of environmental campaigning and trigger a constitutional confrontation with the legislature; completing it would secure electricity for a growing economy."
+ blue_tiger.22.a: "Halt construction"
+ blue_tiger.22.b: "Finish the plant"
+ blue_tiger.22.c: "Refer the dispute to the Grand Justices"
+ blue_tiger.23.t: "Special Defense Budget Showdown"
+ blue_tiger.23.d: "The arms package needs a special budget, and the Legislative Yuan will decide how much of it survives. Supporters call it the minimum for deterrence; critics call it a payment to Washington for weapons we cannot crew."
+ blue_tiger.23.a: "Pass the budget in full"
+ blue_tiger.23.b: "Accept a trimmed budget"
+ blue_tiger.23.c: "Let the budget stall"
+ blue_tiger.24.t: "The HF-2E Controversy"
+ blue_tiger.24.d: "Our engineers have a land-attack cruise missile ready for production. Beijing calls it proof of offensive intent, Washington has asked us privately to reconsider, and the opposition questions its cost."
+ blue_tiger.24.a: "Fund full production"
+ blue_tiger.24.b: "Cap the range and numbers"
+ blue_tiger.24.c: "Shelve the program"
+ blue_tiger.25.t: "Reserve Readiness Audit"
+ blue_tiger.25.d: "The audit is in. Millions of reservists exist on paper, but few have trained since their conscription, and many units lack modern equipment. The question is what to do with the findings."
+ blue_tiger.25.a: "Fund refresher training"
+ blue_tiger.25.b: "Prioritise the active forces"
+ blue_tiger.25.c: "Publish the findings"
+ blue_tiger.26.t: "The Submarine Question"
+ blue_tiger.26.d: "Washington approved diesel submarines in 2001, but no American yard builds them and European builders fear Beijing. We can wait for a solution or begin learning to build our own."
+ blue_tiger.26.a: "Wait for an American solution"
+ blue_tiger.26.b: "Plan an indigenous program"
+ blue_tiger.27.t: "Washington Warns Taipei"
+ blue_tiger.27.d: "The U.S. government has publicly stated that it opposes unilateral changes to the status quo. American officials want our assurance that the latest step will go no further."
+ blue_tiger.27.a: "Give Washington its assurance"
+ blue_tiger.27.b: "Proceed regardless"
+ blue_tiger.28.t: "Deep-Green Discontent"
+ blue_tiger.28.d: "Independence activists in our own camp accuse the government of abandoning its principles to please Washington. They are threatening to sit out the next election."
+ blue_tiger.28.a: "Offer symbolic gestures"
+ blue_tiger.28.b: "Hold the line"
+ TAI_dotcom_bust: "Dot-Com Bust"
+ TAI_dotcom_bust_desc: "Falling global demand for electronics has pushed our export economy into recession.\n§W--------------§!\nThis national spirit is shorter if we complete the §Y$TAI_su_2001_recession$§! focus first."
+ TAI_sars_outbreak: "SARS Outbreak"
+ TAI_sars_outbreak_desc: "A new respiratory epidemic is straining our hospitals and keeping shoppers and tourists at home."
+ TAI_disputed_result: "Disputed Election Result"
+ TAI_disputed_result_desc: "Many citizens doubt the narrow result of the last presidential election.\n§W--------------§!\nThis national spirit will be §RRemoved§! if we complete the §Y$TAI_su_heal_divided_island$§! focus."
+ TAI_reconciliation_success_tt: "§G35%§!: Lien and Soong agree on a joint campaign. The §YKuomintang§! gains popularity at the expense of the §YPeople First Party§!."
+ TAI_reconciliation_failure_tt: "§R65%§!: The talks collapse. The §YPeople First Party§! gains popularity."
+ # Operation Blue Tiger milestone 3
+ blue_tiger.40.t: "Talks with Beijing"
+ blue_tiger.40.d: "Beijing has set out terms for ending the crisis: an end to the blockade in exchange for economic arrangements now and political talks later. Entering talks commits us only to the first stage, and we can leave at any point."
+ blue_tiger.40.a: "Open economic talks"
+ blue_tiger.40.b: "Refuse. The island endures"
+ blue_tiger.41.t: "Economic Talks"
+ blue_tiger.41.d: "Negotiators have agreed on trade, investment and shipping arrangements that would end the blockade. Beijing now proposes a political conference on the island's future."
+ blue_tiger.41.a: "Proceed to a political conference"
+ blue_tiger.41.b: "Keep the talks to trade"
+ blue_tiger.41.c: "Withdraw from the talks"
+ blue_tiger.42.t: "The Political Conference"
+ blue_tiger.42.d: "Delegations are drafting a framework for the island's political future. Under our constitution and the principle of assent, no agreement can take effect unless the people of Taiwan approve it."
+ blue_tiger.42.a: "Put the agreement to a referendum"
+ blue_tiger.42.b: "Withdraw from the conference"
+ blue_tiger.43.t: "The Settlement Referendum"
+ blue_tiger.43.d: "Voters will decide whether to accept the agreement negotiated with Beijing. The result will turn on how badly the crisis has hurt and how strongly citizens identify with the island."
+ blue_tiger.43.a: "Count the votes"
+ blue_tiger.44.t: "The Island Refuses"
+ blue_tiger.44.d: "The agreement has been rejected at the ballot box. The government has a clear mandate to keep the island's future in its own hands, and the result is being read closely in Washington and Tokyo."
+ blue_tiger.44.a: "The people have spoken"
+ blue_tiger.46.t: "Taipei Rejects Our Terms"
+ blue_tiger.46.d: "Taiwan has refused or abandoned the talks we offered. We can tighten the pressure again, or accept the status quo for now and wait for a better moment."
+ blue_tiger.46.a: "Tighten the pressure"
+ blue_tiger.46.b: "Accept the status quo for now"
+ blue_tiger.47.t: "Taipei Opens Talks"
+ blue_tiger.47.d: "Taiwan's negotiators have accepted our invitation to economic talks. Easing the blockade would show good faith; keeping it in place would keep up the pressure on the political stage that follows."
+ blue_tiger.47.a: "Ease the blockade"
+ blue_tiger.47.b: "Keep up the pressure"
+ blue_tiger.50.t: "War in the Strait"
+ blue_tiger.50.d: "The People's Liberation Army has opened hostilities against Taiwan. Missiles are striking airbases and ports, and the fleet is massing across the Strait. Everything prepared in peacetime will now be tested."
+ blue_tiger.50.a: "Execute the Blue Tiger Emergency Doctrine"
+ blue_tiger.50.b: "Mobilise the nation"
+ blue_tiger.51.t: "War in the Taiwan Strait"
+ blue_tiger.51.d: "China has attacked Taiwan. The Taiwan Relations Act lets us provide defensive arms but does not oblige us to fight. Whether we intervene depends on how far we are committed to deterring Beijing and how much we trust Taipei."
+ blue_tiger.51.a: "Defend Taiwan"
+ blue_tiger.51.b: "Send arms and impose sanctions"
+ blue_tiger.51.c: "Stay out of the war"
+ blue_tiger.52.t: "Taipei Seeks Mediation"
+ blue_tiger.52.d: "Taiwan has asked third countries to broker a ceasefire. Our forces have not taken the island, and every week of war costs us at home and abroad."
+ blue_tiger.52.a: "Accept a ceasefire"
+ blue_tiger.52.b: "Fight on"
+ blue_tiger.53.t: "Taipei Requests Support"
+ blue_tiger.53.d: "Taiwan is under heavy pressure from Beijing and has asked for our help. A visible response would reassure Taipei and raise tensions with China; a quiet one would do less of both."
+ blue_tiger.53.a: "Send a carrier group and supplies"
+ blue_tiger.53.b: "Offer quiet diplomatic backing"
+ blue_tiger.53.c: "Decline the request"
+ blue_tiger.55.t: "Beijing Rejects Mediation"
+ blue_tiger.55.d: "Beijing has turned down the ceasefire proposal. The war goes on, but the offer has strengthened our case abroad."
+ blue_tiger.55.a: "We will hold"
+ TAI_american_assistance: "American Assistance"
+ TAI_american_assistance_desc: "Arms, intelligence and supplies from the United States are reaching our forces. It is help, not an alliance."
+ TAI_talks_stage_one_tt: "Economic talks begin. In §Y60§! days we decide whether to move to a political conference, keep talking about trade, or withdraw."
+ TAI_talks_stage_two_tt: "A political conference opens. In §Y90§! days we decide whether to hold a referendum or withdraw."
+ TAI_referendum_called_tt: "A referendum on the agreement is held in §Y30§! days. Approval becomes likelier as §YPressure to Negotiate§! rises and less likely as §YTaiwan-Centered Identity§! rises."
+ TAI_referendum_approved_tt: "If voters §Rapprove§!: Taiwan accepts unification with the mainland."
+ TAI_referendum_rejected_tt: "If voters §Greject§!: the talks end and the government gains a mandate to resist."
+ TAI_blue_tiger_category: "Blue Tiger Emergency"
+ TAI_blue_tiger_category_desc: "Blockade Burden: §Y[?TAI_blockade_burden|0]§!\nPressure to Negotiate: §Y[?TAI_pressure_to_negotiate|0]§!\nU.S. Confidence in Taipei: §Y[?TAI_us_confidence|0]§!\nSemiconductor Supply Security: §Y[?TAI_semiconductor_security|0]§!\n\nBlockade Burden measures how much of Beijing's blockade gets through our preparations. While it is above zero, Pressure to Negotiate rises every month. At §Y70§!, with the blockade still biting, Beijing's terms reach the government."
+ TAI_blockade_burden: "§YBlockade Burden§!"
+ TAI_blockade_burden_tt: "$TAI_blockade_burden$: $RIGHT|-=0$"
+ TAI_declare_bt_emergency: "Declare a Blue Tiger Emergency"
+ TAI_declare_bt_emergency_desc: "Time-limited emergency powers, renewed only by a new decision, let ministries coordinate rationing, shipping and defense."
+ TAI_release_fuel_reserve: "Release the Strategic Fuel Reserve"
+ TAI_release_fuel_reserve_desc: "Drawing down the reserve buys time now. It must be rebuilt once the crisis passes."
+ TAI_rebuild_fuel_reserve: "Rebuild the Strategic Fuel Reserve"
+ TAI_rebuild_fuel_reserve_desc: "With the sea lanes open again, we can refill the tanks we drained."
+ TAI_guarantee_shipping: "Guarantee Commercial Shipping"
+ TAI_guarantee_shipping_desc: "The National Marine Insurance Pool covers ships that private insurers will no longer take, for a premium the treasury pays."
+ TAI_guarantee_shipping_tt: "§YBlockade Burden§! is reduced by §G10§! for §Y180§! days."
+ TAI_ration_energy: "Ration Industrial Energy"
+ TAI_ration_energy_desc: "Cutting industrial power use stretches our fuel and keeps homes and hospitals running."
+ TAI_ration_energy_tt: "§YBlockade Burden§! is reduced by §G5§! for §Y120§! days."
+ TAI_emergency_air_freight: "Emergency Air Freight"
+ TAI_emergency_air_freight_desc: "Aircraft can bring in chip materials and medicine, though never bulk fuel or food."
+ TAI_request_us_support: "Request American Support"
+ TAI_request_us_support_desc: "We can ask Washington for help. What it sends depends on its commitment to deterring Beijing and its confidence in us."
+ TAI_request_japan_credit: "Request Japanese Credit Guarantees"
+ TAI_request_japan_credit_desc: "Pre-arranged credit lines with Japanese lenders keep imports flowing. The money is a loan and adds to our debt."
+ TAI_publicize_incidents: "Publicize PRC Incidents"
+ TAI_publicize_incidents_desc: "Publishing evidence of every incursion and inspection builds support abroad, and raises tension with Beijing."
+ TAI_quiet_protest: "Lodge a Quiet Protest"
+ TAI_quiet_protest_desc: "A private protest through intermediaries registers our objection without inflaming the situation."
+ TAI_seek_mediation: "Seek International Mediation"
+ TAI_seek_mediation_desc: "With Taipei still in our hands, we can ask third countries to broker a ceasefire."
+ TAI_burden_above_19_tt: "§YBlockade Burden§! is at least §Y20§!"
+ TAI_burden_above_39_tt: "§YBlockade Burden§! is at least §Y40§!"
+ TAI_no_blockade_tt: "No blockade is in force"
+ TAI_us_confidence_above_39_tt: "§YU.S. Confidence in Taipei§! is at least §Y40§!"
+ TAI_under_pressure_tt: "§YBlockade Burden§! is at least §Y20§!, or Strait Tension is at least §Y60§!"
+ TAI_ceasefire_tt: "Beijing agrees to a §Ywhite peace§!."
+ CHI_TAI_offer_settlement: "Offer Taiwan an Economic Settlement"
+ CHI_TAI_offer_settlement_desc: "Offer to end the blockade in exchange for economic talks. Any political settlement would still need the agreement of Taiwan's voters."
+ CHI_TAI_settlement_ready_tt: "§YTaiwan§! has §YPressure to Negotiate§! of at least §Y50§!, is not already in talks, and has not recently refused our terms"
+ CHI_TAI_settlement_talks_tt: "§YTaiwan§! enters staged talks that it can leave at any point."
+ TAI_strait_war: "We have been at war with China"
